<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mimar Sinan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1490–<a href="/years/1588">1588</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mimar Sinan was the chief architect of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> in the sixteenth century, serving under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suleiman-the-magnificent">Suleiman the Magnificent</a> and his successors. He designed hundreds of buildings, including the Suleymaniye Mosque in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/istanbul">Istanbul</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/selimiye-mosque">Selimiye Mosque</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edirne">Edirne</a>. His work defined classical Ottoman architecture.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mimar-sinan.jpg" alt="Mimar Sinan" width="320" height="185" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mimar Sinan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mimar_Sinan_signature.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
